---
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

interface Props {
	version: string;
}

const { version } = Astro.props;

// The image reads the current version from the database; the Deployment never runs the upgrade itself
const k8sUpgradeJob = `apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: trendz-upgrade
  namespace: trendz
spec:
  backoffLimit: 0
  template:
    spec:
      restartPolicy: Never
      containers:
        - name: trendz-upgrade
          image: thingsboard/trendz:${version}
          env:
            - name: UPGRADE_TRENDZ
              value: "true"
          envFrom:
            - configMapRef:
                name: trendz-app-db-config
          volumeMounts:
            - name: trendz-app-config
              mountPath: /trendz-config-files
      volumes:
        - name: trendz-app-config
          configMap:
            name: trendz-app-config
            items:
              - key: trendz.conf
                path: trendz.conf
              - key: logback.xml
                path: logback.xml`;
const k8sJobLogOutput =
	'Start upgrading Trendz from version …\n…\nCurrent version is …, upgrade is not needed.';
---

<h3>Update image versions</h3>
<p>Set the image versions to <strong>{version}</strong>. Do not apply the files yet.</p>
<ul>
	<li><code>trendz-app-deployment.yml</code>: <code>thingsboard/trendz:{version}</code></li>
	<li><code>trendz-python-executor-deployment.yml</code>: <code>thingsboard/trendz-python-executor:{version}</code></li>
</ul>

<h3>Stop Trendz</h3>
<Code code={`kubectl scale deployment trendz-app-deployment --replicas=0\nkubectl wait --for=delete pod -l app=trendz-app-pod-label --timeout=120s`} lang="bash" />
<p>If the pods are already gone, <code>kubectl wait</code> may print <code>no matching resources found</code>. This is expected.</p>

<h3>Create the upgrade job</h3>
<Code code={k8sUpgradeJob} lang="yaml" title="trendz-upgrade.yml" meta="download='trendz-upgrade.yml'" />
<p>The ConfigMap names, keys and namespace must match your <code>trendz-app-deployment.yml</code>. Installations created before 1.15 use the keys <code>conf</code> and <code>logback</code>.</p>

<h3>Run the upgrade job</h3>
<Code code={`kubectl apply -f trendz-upgrade.yml\nkubectl wait --for=condition=complete job/trendz-upgrade --timeout=900s`} lang="bash" />

<h3>Verify the upgrade</h3>
<Code code="kubectl logs job/trendz-upgrade" lang="bash" />
<p>Expected output:</p>
<Code code={k8sJobLogOutput} lang="text" />

<h3>Delete the job</h3>
<Code code="kubectl delete job trendz-upgrade" lang="bash" />

<h3>Start Trendz</h3>
<Code code={`kubectl apply -f trendz-python-executor-deployment.yml\nkubectl apply -f trendz-app-deployment.yml`} lang="bash" />
<p>If you run more than one pod, restore the replica count:</p>
<Code code="kubectl scale deployment trendz-app-deployment --replicas=<pod-count>" lang="bash" />
